        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-intro">
                <div class="section-eyebrow">Framework</div>
                <h2>Reading bitcoin through the Power Law</h2>
                <p><em>Why this isn&rsquo;t 2013 bitcoin &mdash; and why today&rsquo;s price may be the most useful signal on the chart.</em></p>
            </div>

            <p class="prose">Every cyclical top in bitcoin&rsquo;s history was visible as a top in real time. Every cycle floor was visible as a floor. The pattern isn&rsquo;t subtle when you plot bitcoin&rsquo;s price against its long-run <a href="/the-power-law">Power Law trend</a> &mdash; tops register as measurable deviations above trend; floors register as measurable deviations below it. The chart below plots both across 16 years of price history, plus today&rsquo;s position.</p>

