            <p class="prose">For an investor with a typical decision horizon &mdash; 10 to 15 years &mdash; both bitcoin lines stay meaningfully above both comparators, with the gap measured in multiples rather than basis points. Each comparator&rsquo;s line, compounding from the same amount today, catches bitcoin&rsquo;s only many decades from now; the dates, and how they move with bitcoin&rsquo;s price, are in the methodology at the foot of the page. <em>Even at the 40-year horizon, bitcoin&rsquo;s trendline expected returns remain substantially higher than any conventional stock-market comparator.</em></p>
